#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/autotranslation.rst:159
msgid "Scaling considerations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/autotranslation.rst:161
msgid ""
"**Target languages are the biggest multiplier.** Each additional language"
" increases both worker time per post and the number of websocket "
"broadcasts per post. Reducing the number of target languages is the most "
"effective way to reduce load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/autotranslation.rst:162
msgid ""
"**Websocket traffic scales with languages.** Each target language "
"produces one channel-wide websocket broadcast per translated post. Under "
"high load, the main symptom of saturation is websocket disconnects caused"
" by per-connection send queues filling up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/autotranslation.rst:163
msgid ""
"**Provider latency shapes traffic patterns.** Lower latency means "
"translations complete in quicker bursts, concentrating websocket traffic."
" Higher latency spreads events over time. Monitor provider response times"
" and factor them into your capacity planning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/autotranslation.rst:166
msgid "Monitor with Prometheus"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/autotranslation.rst:168
msgid "Mattermost exposes the following Prometheus metrics for auto-translation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/autotranslation.rst:170
msgid ""
"``mattermost_autotranslation_queue_depth_total`` *(Gauge)* — current "
"tasks waiting in the queue. A steadily rising value means workers can't "
"keep up with incoming posts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/autotranslation.rst:171
msgid ""
"``mattermost_autotranslation_provider_call_duration_seconds`` "
"*(Histogram; labels: provider, result)* — translation provider latency. "
"This is the ``avg_provider_latency_ms`` value used in the formula above. "
"Calculate the average with the following PromQL query:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/autotranslation.rst:179
msgid ""
"``mattermost_autotranslation_worker_task_duration_seconds`` *(Histogram)*"
" — total time for a worker to process one post across all target "
"languages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/autotranslation.rst:182
msgid "Configuration reference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/autotranslation.rst:184
msgid ""
":ref:`Translation workers <administration-guide/configure/site-"
"configuration-settings:translation workers>`: The number of concurrent "
"workers per node. Default is **6**. Increase this value for high-traffic "
"deployments or decrease it to reduce resource consumption."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/autotranslation.rst:185
msgid ""
":ref:`Translation timeout <administration-guide/configure/site-"
"configuration-settings:translation timeout>`: The maximum time in "
"milliseconds for a single translation request. Default is **5000** ms (5 "
"seconds). Increase this value if your translation provider is "
"experiencing timeouts due to network latency or high load."
msgstr ""

